Chapter: ChachaPolySizeGuard
  cites Foreword chapter Aes
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter ChaCha20Poly1305

 Track D item 19, the ChaCha20Poly1305 leg. RFC 8439 fixes the key at 32 bytes
 and the nonce at 12, and nothing below this chapter checked either.

 Guarded because something runs it (red's ruling, extended to this leg
 2026-08-16): codex/test/chacha20poly1305.codex is the RFC 8439 section 2.8.2
 vector and calls both entry points. There is no production caller.

 chacha-init-state builds the ChaCha20 state by CONCATENATION -- four
 constants, then the key words, then the counter, then the nonce words -- and
 chacha-words-from-bytes takes list-length / 4, so a wrong-sized input does not
 fail anywhere. It shifts which words of the state are which.

 Measured on the unguarded chapter before this arm was written:

 A nonce of 16 bytes gives four nonce words, a 17-word state, and the rounds
 and chacha-add-states both stop at 16, so the extra word is dropped and the
 keystream is EXACTLY the keystream of the 12-byte prefix. Two different
 nonces, one keystream. That is Poly1305 nonce reuse, which this chapter's own
 opening says destroys it.

 A key of 64 bytes gives sixteen key words, so words 0..15 are the four
 constants and the first twelve key words and the nonce never enters the state
 at all. Two different nonces then give byte-identical ciphertext.

 A nonce of 11 bytes gives two nonce words and a 15-word state, and
 chacha-qr state 3 7 11 15 reads index 15. The guest dies.

 Rows 1 and 2 are the instrument's control: two legitimate nonces must give
 different ciphertext, or rows 6 and 7 agreeing would prove nothing.

Section: Vector

  k32 : List Integer =
    [128, 129, 130, 131, 132, 133, 134, 135, 136, 137, 138, 139, 140, 141, 142, 143,
     144, 145, 146, 147, 148, 149, 150, 151, 152, 153, 154, 155, 156, 157, 158, 159]

  k64 : List Integer = k32 & k32

  n12 : List Integer = [7, 0, 0, 0, 64, 65, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71]

  n12b : List Integer = [9, 0, 0, 0, 64, 65, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71]

  n16 : List Integer = n12 & [1, 2, 3, 4]

  n11 : List Integer = [7, 0, 0, 0, 64, 65, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70]

  plain : List Integer = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]

  aad : List Integer = [80, 81, 82, 83]

Section: Helpers

  hex : List Integer -> Text
  hex (bs) = hex-loop bs 0 (list-length bs) ""

  hex-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  hex-loop (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else hex-loop bs (i + 1) n (acc & aes-hex-byte (list-at bs i))

  show-bool : Boolean -> Text
  show-bool (b) = if b then "True" else "False"

  enc-row : Text, List Integer, List Integer -> Text
  enc-row (label) (key) (nonce) =
    let r = chacha20poly1305-encrypt key nonce plain aad
    in label & " valid=" & show-bool (r.cp-valid) & " ct=" & hex (r.cp-ciphertext)

  dec-row : Text, List Integer, List Integer -> Text
  dec-row (label) (key) (nonce) =
    let good = chacha20poly1305-encrypt k32 n12 plain aad
    in let d = chacha20poly1305-decrypt key nonce (good.cp-ciphertext) aad (good.cp-tag)
    in when d
      is Just (p) -> label & " decrypt=" & hex p
      is None -> label & " decrypt=REJECTED"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (enc-row "1-key32-nonce12" k32 n12)
    print-line-uni (enc-row "2-key32-nonce12b" k32 n12b)
    print-line-uni (dec-row "3-roundtrip" k32 n12)
    print-line-uni (dec-row "4-wrong-nonce" k32 n12b)
    print-line-uni (enc-row "5-nonce16" k32 n16)
    print-line-uni (enc-row "6-key64-nonce12" k64 n12)
    print-line-uni (enc-row "7-key64-nonce12b" k64 n12b)
    print-line-uni (enc-row "8-nonce11" k32 n11)
    print-line-uni (dec-row "9-decrypt-nonce11" k32 n11)
  end

